From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 02-rights candidate r4: lost logs, CPI and short post-states
 are never a PASS

VR and V7 now meet workstream 11's evidence rules on their own, without
contradicting its V0E:

- A Grant instruction whose record is absent while the logs show they
  were cut, lost their tail, or show no invocation is UNVERIFIABLE
  (MissingData), not RightsRecordMissing; the Grant is then not judged
  past the gap. V7 does the same for the holdings it wrote. With whole
  logs both stay FAILs.
- A Grant record or Grant write from the program run inside another
  program (CPI) is UNVERIFIABLE, not an orphan or unexplained account.
- A program account a Grant instruction holds writable without a
  post-state is UNVERIFIABLE.

Tests: the base fixture's own verdict is FAIL, so "verdict is not PASS"
proved nothing; tests now require the change itself to add a FAIL or an
UNVERIFIABLE finding. New unsigned tests for lost logs (three ways),
whole logs, CPI with and without logs, and short post-states.
ABI numbers, check names and codes stay provisional.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
